  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0040","idiomatic","The rhetorician Cao Qiusheng traded on influence for gold, curried favor with men such as the favorite Zhao Tan, and was close to Dou Zhang, the empress's brother.","The rhetorician Cao Qiusheng repeatedly cultivated influence and sought money, attached himself to prominent men such as Zhao Tan, and befriended Dou Changjun, the empress's elder brother.","The proposal correctly repairs Dou Zhang but wrongly discards a valid identification. Shiji 49 explicitly identifies Dou Changjun as Empress Dou's elder brother.","high","applied"],
    ["s0063","literal","When Peng Yue was a commoner family man, he once roamed with Bu; in poverty and straits, he sold labor in Qi and was a wine-shop guarantor.","When Peng Yue was a commoner family man, he once roamed with Bu; in poverty and straits, they hired out labor in Qi, and Bu was a wine-shop guarantor.","窮困，賣庸於齊，為酒家保 is shared hardship with Bu, and 為酒家保 belongs to Bu (as the parallel idiomatic already has); the proposed 'wine-shop guard' misrenders 保, so keep 'guarantor' while correcting the agent.","medium","applied"]
  ],
